Root help is rendered through utoo's config-aware help view, not clap's default
template. Pin only the stable command list and option labels.

```console
$ utoo --help
...
Usage:
  ut <COMMAND>
...
Commands:
  install          Install project dependencies (i, add)
...
  completions      Generate shell completion scripts (cmp)
...
Options:
  -h, --help       Print help information
  -v, --version    Print version information
...

```

`add` is an alias for `install`, so clap renders the install command help.

```console
$ utoo add --help
Install project dependencies

Usage: utoo[EXE] install [OPTIONS] [SPECS]...
...
      --save-peer
          Save as peer dependency
...
  -h, --help
          Print help

```
